  "note": "Also needs |τ| for τ < 0 (see Theorem 8.0.1). Typo: The first case of (8.4), |x0|>=0.51729 sqrt(tau) 'for rho arbitrary', is false for rho<1.49997, since x0/sqrt(tau)=sqrt((j(rho)-1)/(2rho)) increases (0.34356 at rho=0.5); it should read 'for rho>=3/2', which is what (8.46) proves and the only case Cor 8.0.2 uses. (checked by `scripts/checks/eq_8_4.py`)."
